(5640875, 818230, 104537, '<td valign="top">Remarkable capture. I love the tones in this image. Outstanding!</td>', 'Remarkable capture. I love the tones in this image. Outstanding!', '2009-09-08 20:43:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(5640881, 818612, 104537, '<td valign="top">The light and detail are fantastic in this one.</td>', 'The light and detail are fantastic in this one.', '2009-09-08 20:46:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(5640882, 817539, 104537, '<td valign="top">Outstanding detail.</td>', 'Outstanding detail.', '2009-09-08 20:46:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(5640970, 817057, 83313, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 5, but I think I waffled a bit and almost gave it a 4. I suspect other voters are being harder on it. I see some effort to create an interesting composition, however my eye does not go where I think you intended. The large expanse of shrubbery is brighter than the fence and draws my eye instead. A fence around a home is a difficult subject in the first place, as it not terribly interesting by it''s nature. A different angle perhaps, or a view from the outside might have helped. Or a skywards view of the fence, shot from the ground. (I''m a big fan of <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/portfolio.php?USER_ID=83313&amp;collection_id=32266" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">getting really low</a> for a perspective shot.)<br/> <br/>Working with just this shot, I''d think perhaps a tighter crop on the fence could benefit the composition, using the "rule of thirds" and some adjustments (such as curves, saturation, contrast &amp; sharpening) could help to pull out some more detail and visual pop from the subject.</td>', 'I gave this a 5, but I think I waffled a bit and almost gave it a 4. I suspect other voters are being harder on it. I see some effort to create an interesting composition, however my eye does not go where I think you intended. The large expanse of shrubbery is brighter than the fence and draws my eye instead. A fence around a home is a difficult subject in the first place, as it not terribly interesting by it''s nature. A different angle perhaps, or a view from the outside might have helped. Or a skywards view of the fence, shot from the ground. (I''m a big fan of getting really low for a perspective shot.) Working with just this shot, I''d think perhaps a tighter crop on the fence could benefit the composition, using the "rule of thirds" and some adjustments (such as curves, saturation, contrast & sharpening) could help to pull out some more detail and visual pop from the subject.', '2009-09-08 22:02:41.000000', NULL, 1),
