(5642000, 818617, 38162, '<td valign="top">really eyewave, you need to get over yourself.  learn to be a good winner (or is it spelled whiner?).<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by eyewave:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by levyj413:</b></div><hr/><i> Ah, nothing like seeing the photographer''s comment on the blue basically be "voters suck."<br/> <br/>Since you seem to know your shots deserve to win ribbons, why do you bother giving voters the chance to express an opinion? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Never said voter suck. Wouldn''t you think you''d ribbon at a score of 7.4? Wouldn''t you be disappointed when your score fell as rapidly? And do I always have to use a ;-) icon so you also understand the humor in my comments? </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'really eyewave, you need to get over yourself.  learn to be a good winner (or is it spelled whiner?). Originally posted by eyewave: Originally posted by levyj413: Ah, nothing like seeing the photographer''s comment on the blue basically be "voters suck." Since you seem to know your shots deserve to win ribbons, why do you bother giving voters the chance to express an opinion?   Never said voter suck. Wouldn''t you think you''d ribbon at a score of 7.4? Wouldn''t you be disappointed when your score fell as rapidly? And do I always have to use a ;-) icon so you also understand the humor in my comments? ', '2009-09-09 12:21:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(5642038, 818778, 30049, '<td valign="top">Wow.  I went to the Canon A530 camera page here on DPC and discovered there are 83 people that own this camera.  :-)<br/> <br/>Regarding the photo - I like the perspective you selected.  The angle of the lines gives some nice tension to the image, yet is still easy enough to view without having to lean one way or the other.</td>', 'Wow.  I went to the Canon A530 camera page here on DPC and discovered there are 83 people that own this camera.  :-) Regarding the photo - I like the perspective you selected.  The angle of the lines gives some nice tension to the image, yet is still easy enough to view without having to lean one way or the other.', '2009-09-09 13:29:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(5642119, 818617, 3936, '<td valign="top">Very nicely done, and well deserving of the blue.  I love the way the tones of the sky and the structure work together.</td>', 'Very nicely done, and well deserving of the blue.  I love the way the tones of the sky and the structure work together.', '2009-09-09 14:13:04.000000', NULL, 0),
