(5643281, 817810, 108580, '<td valign="top">Hi Dan, I was torn between a 5 and a 6 on this shot, many got 4''s from me that I thought were horrendous point, shoot, upload attempts, barring about 35-40 shots that I scored 6+. I personally saw 3 lines, the main line of twisted wire as one and then the two twisted together. 1+1=3? The diagonal is appealing to me, bottom left drawing up to focus at middle right. Perhaps a wee bit more focus before and beyond the barb would have you bought you at least more 5+ votes. Another string of wire OOF can be seen BR and that put me off a 6. Still a well judged shot and relevant to the challenge. WD.</td>', 'Hi Dan, I was torn between a 5 and a 6 on this shot, many got 4''s from me that I thought were horrendous point, shoot, upload attempts, barring about 35-40 shots that I scored 6+. I personally saw 3 lines, the main line of twisted wire as one and then the two twisted together. 1+1=3? The diagonal is appealing to me, bottom left drawing up to focus at middle right. Perhaps a wee bit more focus before and beyond the barb would have you bought you at least more 5+ votes. Another string of wire OOF can be seen BR and that put me off a 6. Still a well judged shot and relevant to the challenge. WD.', '2009-09-10 14:52:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(5643286, 817810, 108580, '<td valign="top">I''ve had a thought on this "placement in the challenge" thing and where one places:<br/> <br/>85 of your votes were 5 or more.<br/>65 of your votes were 4 or less.<br/>You also got a 10.<br/> <br/>56% of your votes were above 5, from what I''ve seen at DPC that''s darn good.<br/> <br/>I''m looking at it from this perspective now, i.e. Can I stay above 5. Sure I''d like a ribbon, who wouldn''t, but right now I''m learning as to what''s liked here and what''s not. It however won''t affect my enjoyment of photography.</td>', 'I''ve had a thought on this "placement in the challenge" thing and where one places: 85 of your votes were 5 or more.65 of your votes were 4 or less.You also got a 10. 56% of your votes were above 5, from what I''ve seen at DPC that''s darn good. I''m looking at it from this perspective now, i.e. Can I stay above 5. Sure I''d like a ribbon, who wouldn''t, but right now I''m learning as to what''s liked here and what''s not. It however won''t affect my enjoyment of photography.', '2009-09-10 15:00:43.000000', NULL, 0),
