(5645543, 818787, 28322, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Jaded_Housewife:</b></div><hr/><i> I didn''t vote in the challenge since I was in it and I never vote in challenges I participate it but I did think it was super cute and original. One thing that would have made it better for me would have been if your title was "Mommy makes me pull my hair". Would have made the I love daddy shirt soooooooo much funnier. Even better if she was sitting in front of a plate of peas or something with mommy pointing as if telling her to eat them. something like that. Just to give the photo a story. Hoestly, TONS of my pictures don''t have stories. Just trying to troubleshoot why it scored low. <br/>HTH. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I so agree with you about the name, Mommy in the title Daddy on the shirt would''ve made it stronger and more appealing :) Thanks for you suggestion, it is indeed a wonderful point, <br/>Regards :)</td>', 'Originally posted by Jaded_Housewife: I didn''t vote in the challenge since I was in it and I never vote in challenges I participate it but I did think it was super cute and original. One thing that would have made it better for me would have been if your title was "Mommy makes me pull my hair". Would have made the I love daddy shirt soooooooo much funnier. Even better if she was sitting in front of a plate of peas or something with mommy pointing as if telling her to eat them. something like that. Just to give the photo a story. Hoestly, TONS of my pictures don''t have stories. Just trying to troubleshoot why it scored low. HTH.   I so agree with you about the name, Mommy in the title Daddy on the shirt would''ve made it stronger and more appealing :) Thanks for you suggestion, it is indeed a wonderful point, Regards :)', '2009-09-13 17:51:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(5645708, 818755, 554, '<td valign="top">Well Robin, you have pretty much answered your own question.  Looks like a shoehorn entry and has a poor choice of background.  The rotation didn''t help.  The water spirts don''t screem "lines", and without the title who''d a guessed.<br/>In your favor though, the pink thing is focused well and the water does make a nice interesting subject, for the one taking the shot and trying to stop the motion, which you did.<br/>I didn''t vote but if I had it would have been a 5.  Depending on my mood it might have been 4, (probably a 5).  Everybody has their own scale but I find it hard to see a 1 or 2 here as well as an 8, 9, or 10.<br/>"Not actually taken for the challenge" says a lot.<br/> <br/>Good luck in future challenges and keep on entering...David</td>', 'Well Robin, you have pretty much answered your own question.  Looks like a shoehorn entry and has a poor choice of background.  The rotation didn''t help.  The water spirts don''t screem "lines", and without the title who''d a guessed.In your favor though, the pink thing is focused well and the water does make a nice interesting subject, for the one taking the shot and trying to stop the motion, which you did.I didn''t vote but if I had it would have been a 5.  Depending on my mood it might have been 4, (probably a 5).  Everybody has their own scale but I find it hard to see a 1 or 2 here as well as an 8, 9, or 10."Not actually taken for the challenge" says a lot. Good luck in future challenges and keep on entering...David', '2009-09-13 20:40:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(5645731, 818755, 83313, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 5. I saw a good effort to capture an interesting shot, but the image is a little flat.  The background appears tilted, and distracts from the main subject. I think it has some potential though, and I did a quick edit to see what I could pull from it. I think by fixing the tilt and cropping, the background was reduced as a distracting element, and might even be a secondary point of interest. I kind of like the way it looks like colorful strata.<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=820981" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/83313/120/820981.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/83313/120/820981.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/83313/120/820981.jpg"/></a></td>', 'I gave this a 5. I saw a good effort to capture an interesting shot, but the image is a little flat.  The background appears tilted, and distracts from the main subject. I think it has some potential though, and I did a quick edit to see what I could pull from it. I think by fixing the tilt and cropping, the background was reduced as a distracting element, and might even be a secondary point of interest. I kind of like the way it looks like colorful strata.', '2009-09-13 20:54:21.000000', NULL, 0),
